{
  "constants": {
    "L": 10,
    "F": 3,
    "W": 15,
    "I": 400
  },
  "setups": {
    "create": "The card under test is LOADED by CREATE with the right access hash (any 32-byte value; the wrong access hash is any other value), followed by a new OPEN: f = 0, waited = 0, not verified.",
    "set": "Two cards personalized under one CA: the member Y and the card under test X. Y is LOADED by CREATE P1 = 01 with the right access hash, any valid seed and ID(X) as the other member. X (BLANK) answers OFFER; Y exports to X (EXPORT P1 = 00 with X's certificate and that OFFER response, EXPORT P1 = 01 with the right access hash); X answers IMPORT P1 = 00 and P1 = 01 with 9000. Then a new OPEN on X: X is LOADED with Y's wallet (members Y, X), f = 0, waited = 0, not verified, offer = NONE."
  },
  "stepRules": "After a step that has status the replayer sends STATUS in the current session of the card under test and compares its response with status (life(1) \u2016 tries(1), \u00a79.3); STATUS has no side effect on the card but, like every command that does not continue it, ends a pending import (\u00a79.2), so steps that leave one for the next step have no status. A step with repeat n is sent n times, each answered with sw; status is checked after the last one. Codes: right is the access hash of the setup, wrong any other, new a third access hash. OFFER: lk new means the returned LK differs from every LK the card returned before, same that it equals the LK of the previous OFFER. EXPORT runs on the member Y, not on the card under test: a new OPEN on Y, VERIFY with the right code, EXPORT P1 = 00 with X's certificate and X's most recent OFFER response, then EXPORT P1 = 01 with the access hash named by code; both return sw, and the exports of a sequence are numbered 1, 2, \u2026 in order. IMPORT0 sends IMPORT P1 = 00 with Y's certificate and the E \u2016 sig_S of export number export (default: the latest); IMPORT1 sends IMPORT P1 = 01 with the ct \u2016 tag of the export of the pending import, or of the latest export when there is none.",
  "tear": "after-T-FAIL: power is lost after the T-FAIL transaction of this VERIFY committed and before any later persistent write (\u00a79.5 steps 5-9). The command has no response (sw torn); the replayer powers the card up, SELECTs the wallet applet and OPENs a new session before the STATUS check.",
  "sequences": [
